    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI support chatbot that answers from your own pages\n\n**Who it's for:** small businesses and support teams that answer the same customer questions every day.\n\n**What it does**\n1. **Load content** (bottom): fetches your public pages, keeps the readable text, splits it into passages and stores them in a knowledge base.\n2. **Answer** (top): a chat widget sends each question to an AI agent. The agent searches the knowledge base first and answers only from what it finds.\n3. If the answer isn't in your pages, the customer is told a person will follow up and your team gets a **Slack alert**.\n4. Every question, reply and handoff is **logged to Google Sheets**.\n\n**Embed it:** open *When chat message received*, copy the chat URL, or switch the mode to *Embedded Chat* and use n8n's chat widget snippet on your site.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 640
      },
      "id": "c273a327-d198-4ed6-ad62-1e5fd15190d6",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -420,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Setup (about 15 minutes)\n1. **Content:** in *Pages to learn from*, list your FAQ, pricing, shipping and returns pages. Run *Load or refresh content* once (and again after you change your site).\n2. **Embeddings:** add an OpenAI credential to both *Embeddings* nodes (same model in both).\n3. **AI model:** add an Anthropic credential to *Claude model*. Haiku keeps cost low; any chat model node works.\n4. **Google Sheets:** make a sheet with a `Chats` tab and the header row `date, sessionId, question, reply, handedOff`. Paste its URL in *Log conversation*.\n5. **Slack:** connect Slack and pick the channel in *Alert the team*.\n6. Set an n8n variable `BUSINESS_NAME`, or edit the agent's system message.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "43112523-9a36-4c00-ab58-7b8453970a3a",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -420,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Going live\nThe *Simple Vector Store* lives in n8n's memory and is cleared on restart. For production, swap both knowledge-base nodes for Pinecone, Qdrant, Supabase or Postgres (PGVector) with the same settings. Nothing else changes.",
        "width": 360,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "7fd21622-8ed0-4851-9147-ddde09667947",
      "name": "Production note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1180,
        420
      ]
    }
